### 7. Inline Edit (`inlineEdit`)

**Purpose**: Enable inline editing of text fields with optimistic updates.

**Usage**:
```html
<div x-data="inlineEdit('Initial value', '/tasks/123', 'title')">
  <div x-show="!editing" class="group">
    <span x-text="value"></span>
    <button @click="startEdit" class="btn-ghost opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100">
      Edit
    </button>
  </div>

  <div x-show="editing">
    <input type="text"
           x-model="value"
           @keydown="handleKeydown" />
    <button @click="save" :disabled="saving">Save</button>
    <button @click="cancel">Cancel</button>
  </div>
</div>
```

**Properties**:
- `editing` (boolean): Edit mode state
- `value` (string): Current value
- `originalValue` (string): Backup for cancel
- `saving` (boolean): Save operation in progress
- `error` (string|null): Error message
- `startEdit()`: Enter edit mode
- `save()`: Save changes via PATCH request
- `cancel()`: Cancel and restore original value
- `handleKeydown(e)`: Handle Enter (save) and Escape (cancel)

**API**: Sends `PATCH` request to endpoint with JSON body: `{ [field]: value }`

