### 9. Confirmation Dialog (`confirmDialog`)

**Purpose**: Confirm destructive actions before execution.

**Usage**:
```html
<div x-data="confirmDialog">
  <button @click="show({
    title: 'Delete Task',
    message: 'Are you sure?',
    confirmText: 'Delete',
    onConfirm: () => deleteTask()
  })">
    Delete
  </button>

  <div x-show="open" class="modal modal-open">
    <div class="modal-box">
      <h3 x-text="title"></h3>
      <p x-text="message"></p>
      <div class="modal-action">
        <button @click="confirm" x-text="confirmText"></button>
        <button @click="close" x-text="cancelText"></button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
```

**Properties**:
- `open` (boolean): Dialog visibility
- `title` (string): Dialog title
- `message` (string): Confirmation message
- `confirmText` (string): Confirm button text
- `cancelText` (string): Cancel button text
- `onConfirm` (function): Callback on confirmation
- `show(options)`: Display dialog
- `confirm()`: Execute callback and close
- `close()`: Close dialog

